[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1280","stub":{"id":"1280","section":"1. Wakeley Dam to Spraque Brook","altname":"","river":"Cedar","difficulty":"IItoV","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"4.17","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108652","location":{"latitude":"43.7296981811523","longitude":"-74.4728012084961"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"113887","location":{"latitude":"43.7863998413086","longitude":"-74.2957992553711"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"3923","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5868","description":"","caption":"Body Snatcher","poi_name":"Body Snatcher","subject":"Body Snatcher","author":"Bob Spooner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3923","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3923"}},{"id":"3926","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5868","description":"","caption":"A beautiful spring day in the 'dacks","poi_name":"","subject":"Paul Griese","author":"Bob Spooner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3926","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3926"}},{"id":"3924","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5868","description":"","caption":"Last rapid on Cedar","poi_name":"","subject":"Casey McCormick","author":"Bob Spooner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3924","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3924"}},{"id":"3927","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5868","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":"the second to the last drop","subject":"Peter Gaddy","author":"Bob Spooner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3927","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3927"}},{"id":"3922","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5868","description":"","caption":"Ben B","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Bob Spooner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3922","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3922"}},{"id":"3925","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5868","description":"","caption":"Gorge","poi_name":"","subject":"Gorge down stream of body snatcher","author":"Bob Spooner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3925","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3925"}}],"detail":{"id":"1280","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Wakely Dam Road is not plowed. Put in at the dam and take out at the parking lot at the beginning of the unmaintained road to Wakely Dam. Take out on the left when you see the cable across the river for the class V section. From the parking lot down to the road is class II-III.\n\nRobert Farmer shared:\n\nIt has been a few years since I did this... I remember fondly camping out on a freezing night with a strong wind at the lake above the dam, with a brilliant moon floating over the surface of the lake. It was a week when most rivers were way too high. I remember looking at some multi-syllabic rivers with sheer terror and regret that I had driven all that way, possibly for nothing. But then I heard about the Cedar. There were a few easy, entrance rapids below the dam for a half-mile or so, then I recall a large left turn with a small slide. I was kind of on edge because the description that I had received from Bones, at Whitewater Challengers, was a bit vague. But when I got to the entrance of the mini-gorge, it was obvious. The river narrowed to about 15 feet against a vertical wall on the right. The left side had an elevated shelf about 8 (?) feet wide against a vertical wall on the left. Near the bottom was an undercut on the right that looked to be about 25 feet deep, or more. This section was a portage, but I still wanted to run it, until I saw it. I portaged, with no regrets. But, with a ton of water, the portage route would be underwater, with vertical walls on both sides. Eeyowza!\n\nAt the end of the portage shelf, the gorge makes a 90-degree left turn, then a 90-degree right turn, i.e. there was no visibility. Putting back in requires a seal-launch to total commitment to a blind gorge, the upper part of which was terrifying, that was essentially completely unknown except for a vague description from a guy named \"Bones.\" Not greatly encouraging! I had to think about that for a good, long while. But I put in, and it was good. The gorge opened up a bit before another thrilling and runnable rapid---with a suspicious curling wave---that I scouted very intently before running it with great intensity. I vaguely recall that the river was much easier after this. There was probably a takeout around here that I missed. I went downstream past a mini-mansion, then ran a 15+-foot dam with a slight angle to avoid pitoning at the bottom, then past a few miles of easy water to where I had parked by the side of the road.\n\nThe mini-gorge is pretty amazing, and makes the trip worth the trouble. But, anyway, if you're considering this because it is running and you're in the neighborhood, just accept the idea that you're going to do it, because probably nothing else will be low enough for you to run, anyway. The Cedar is pretty cool, albeit short, but still worth the trouble.--RF\n\n**Eastern Adirondacks Reaches**\n\n[Ausable, E. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1238/) [Ausable, W. Branch (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1241/) [Ausable, W. Branch (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1239/) [Balm of Gilead Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/2996/)\n\n[Boquet (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1261/) [Boquet (3.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1262/) [Boquet, N. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1264/)[Boquet, S. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1263/)\n\n[Boreas (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1266/) [Branch, The (Boquet trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1441/) [Branch, The (Schroon trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1442/) [Cedar (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1280/)\n\n[Cedar (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1281/) [Cold](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1287/) [Deer Creek (Hudson Trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1184/)[Glen Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1309/)\n\n[Hague Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10876/) [Hudson (0.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10653/) [Hudson (1. Indian River to North River)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1321/) [Hudson (2. North River to Riparius)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1322/)\n\n[Hudson (3. Riparius to the Glen)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1323/) [Indian (Hudson trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1325/) [John's Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/2913/)[La Chute](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1335/)\n\n[Mettawee](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1343/)[Mill Creek (Essex County](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4251/))                    [Mill Creek (Hudson trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1346/) [North Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4303/)\n\n[Pike Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10886/) [Poultney](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1383/)[Putnam Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4253/) [Raquette (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1385/)\n\n[Rock River](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1391/) [Schroon (North Hudson to Schroon Falls)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1422/) [Schroon (Starbuckville to Riverbank)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1423/)[Schroon (Warrensburg to Thurman Station)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1421/)\n\n[Squaw Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3886/) [Styles Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4281/) [Thirteenth Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1443/) [Trout brook (Schroon trib)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3284/)\n\n[West Mill Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4314/)\n\n**[Google Map of New York Whitewater](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)**\n\n**[New York Whitewater Paddlers Facebook Group](https://www.facebook.com/groups/108070075877312/)**","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"13.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"1280","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":n